  "id": "least-effort-principle",
  "term": "least effort principle",
  "definition": "The least effort principle is the idea that people tend to organize language use to reduce effort while still communicating successfully. In the packet, it refers to a balance between efficiency and accuracy, helping explain why shorter forms are often used more frequently but are also shaped by other pressures.",
